findings.recommendation:
Add a guard in nginx that explicitly rejects empty auth values:
```nginx
# Reject empty or missing Authorization header before variable comparison
if ($http_authorization = "") {
    return 401 '{"error":"unauthorized"}';
}
if ($memory_api_key = "") {
    # Emergency lockout if secret file misconfigured
    return 503 '{"error":"service_unavailable"}';
}
```
Alternatively, the setup instructions could be strengthened to verify the secrets file before nginx reload.

Optional for single-user deployment. If monitoring is needed, add:
```nginx
log_format memory_api '$remote_addr - [$time_local] "$request" $status $body_bytes_sent "$http_user_agent" rt=$request_time';
access_log /var/log/nginx/memory-access.log memory_api;
```
Notice: Authorization header value is NOT included (would log the Bearer token).
